    {
      "id": "claim_1f262d2cb9d44aff9d93e2613738bae8",
      "statement": "internal/cmd/auth_options.go centralizes CLI flag/option plumbing shared by every authenticating command: addOutputFlag/commandOutput register and validate the -o/--output flag, tokenOptions builds the auth.Options value (including UseDeviceCode from the resolved profile) passed to every token-acquisition call, and configureDeviceCode lets config init set a saved device-flow preference only from an explicit --use-device-code=true, never inherited from an existing profile or environment.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/cmd/auth_options.go#L1-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1db4541d12f1d8ea4a8d518bb00aa195a6717e6bab199de39e8270c3dff13e89:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_23da56bbe30a421cb998505103dce9f4",
      "statement": "All PKCE and device-code token acquisition, caching, and clearing is owned by the internal/auth package (oidc.go, device.go, callback.go, token.go); internal/cmd/root.go's assumeRoleWithRetryOptions and isAuthError orchestrate retries by calling into that package (CachedTokenForConfig, GetTokenWithOptions, ClearToken) rather than implementing the flows, and internal/cmd/cli.go's commandPreRun only resolves configuration and selects which role to assume before delegating to assumeRoleWithRetryOptions.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/auth/oidc.go#L57-L103",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:889ec4a9ad2730aa55ec8e767c33bda163d29dd949a0ca4d66afdb36d949a7ff:"
        },
        {
