        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_99721fdd7dc54a3780617a72943dbfa5",
      "statement": "The ID token cache in internal/auth/token.go is scoped per OIDC issuer and client ID (CachedTokenForConfig/SaveTokenForConfig), so switching profiles or issuers never reuses another deployment's cached token and a legacy unscoped cache is not trusted once a profile is configured; the cache file is written mode 0600 with permissions re-applied via os.Chmod on every write.",
      "evidence": [
